 "evaluation": "All three responses rightly identify the disagreement as genuine, with primary differences in population (children and adolescents with vitamin D deficiency vs adults aged 18-60) and secondary differences in intervention (2640 IU/day for 28 days + TAU vs 50,000 IU every 2 weeks for 8 weeks). Response B is the most accurate because it leaves out extraneous `also_differs` tags and accurately puts co-treatment (TAU) under intervention. Response A adds `comparator` (presumably for placebo + TAU vs placebo, which is minimal/redundant with co-treatment under intervention), while Response C adds `design_or_bias` even though both are placebo-controlled RCTs with no reported bias.",
 "ranking": [
  "B",
  "A",
  "C"
 ]
}
